<Docs title="Keybinding Reference" description="Complete keybinding reference for grüt — global, navigation, file tree, git info, GitHub, commits, and preview panels.">
  <h1>Keybinding Reference</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    All default keybindings organized by context. grüt ships with three
    keybinding schemes — <code>default</code>, <code>vim</code>, and
    <code>classic</code> — configurable via <code>keybinding_scheme</code> in
    your config.
  </p>

  <Screenshot src="/grut/screenshots/default/help.png" alt="Help overlay showing keybinding reference" caption="Help overlay with keybinding reference (press ? to open)" />

  <h2>Global</h2>
  <p>These bindings work everywhere, regardless of the focused panel.</p>
  <KeybindingTable bindings={[
    { key: '1', action: 'Focus File Tree panel' },
    { key: '2', action: 'Focus Git Info panel' },
    { key: '3', action: 'Focus GitHub panel' },
    { key: '4', action: 'Focus Commits panel' },
    { key: '5', action: 'Focus Preview panel' },
    { key: 'Tab', action: 'Focus next panel' },
    { key: 'Shift+Tab', action: 'Focus previous panel' },
    { key: 'R', action: 'Refresh all data + preview' },
    { key: 'P', action: 'Push' },
    { key: 'F', action: 'Fetch all remotes' },
    { key: '?', action: 'Help overlay' },
    { key: 'Ctrl+g', action: 'Git command log' },
    { key: ',', action: 'Settings' },
    { key: '/', action: 'Fuzzy finder' },
    { key: ':', action: 'Command palette' },
    { key: '~', action: 'Change directory' },
    { key: 'Ctrl+c', action: 'Quit' },
    { key: 'Ctrl+Space', action: 'Toggle AI chat' },
    { key: 'Ctrl+z', action: 'Undo last git action' },
    { key: 'Ctrl+y', action: 'Redo' },
  ]} />

