  <h2>Keybinding Schemes</h2>
  <p>
    grüt supports three keybinding schemes. The bindings listed above are the
    <code>default</code> scheme. You can switch schemes in your config:
  </p>
  <pre><code>[general]
keybinding_scheme = "vim"   # "default" | "vim" | "classic"</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>default</strong> — the bindings shown on this page</li>
    <li><strong>vim</strong> — vim-style motions with additional <code>dd</code>, <code>yy</code>, and visual-mode-style selection</li>
    <li><strong>classic</strong> — keybindings for users who prefer classic TUI conventions</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    All schemes share the same global bindings (<kbd>Ctrl+c</kbd>,
    <kbd>?</kbd>, <kbd>Tab</kbd>, number keys). The differences are in
    navigation and git operation keys.
  </p>
</Docs>

